From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 22:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: check ACPI DSM support before evaluation

Avoid evaluating a device ACPI _DSM function unless firmware actually
advertises it.  The availability check also prevents firmware warnings
on Orion O6 systems whose wireless device does not implement the
Realtek DSM interface.

Three pre-flight guards added to rtw89_acpi_evaluate_dsm():
  1. NULL-handle check -- if the ACPI_HANDLE is NULL, the device has
     no ACPI companion and _DSM cannot be evaluated; return -ENOENT
     instead of calling acpi_evaluate_dsm() on a NULL handle.
  2. func >= 64 sanity check -- the DSM function index is a 6-bit
     bitmap; values >= 64 are nonsense.  Return -ENOENT before
     issuing a wild-index call to acpi_evaluate_dsm().
  3. acpi_check_dsm() -- query the firmware-advertised DSM bitmap for
     the rtw89 GUID.  If the requested function bit is not set,
     return -ENOENT without ever invoking acpi_evaluate_dsm().

Behavior change: previously rtw89_acpi_evaluate_dsm() unconditionally
called acpi_evaluate_dsm(); on firmware that did not advertise the
_DSM at all, this generated ACPI warnings ("_DSM evaluate failed")
even though the driver would have handled the missing DSM anyway.
The new path is functionally equivalent on the failure path and
quiet on the ACPI subsystem in the common no-DSM case.

Not Orion-specific and not CIX-specific -- a generic robustness
improvement to the rtw89 driver's ACPI path.  Carries essentially
no risk; aligns rtw89 with the upstream-recommended
acpi_check_dsm() pattern used by most other kernel drivers.

Ported from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds:
  sys-kernel/cix-sources/files/7.2.x/80020-rtw89-check-acpi-dsm-before-evaluating.patch

Signed-off-by: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
[ported: applied verbatim from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds 7.2.x/]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/acpi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/acpi.c
index ebb6cf555..5e4b8b104 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/acpi.c
@@ -372,11 +372,18 @@ int rtw89_acpi_evaluate_dsm(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev,
 			    enum rtw89_acpi_dsm_func func,
 			    struct rtw89_acpi_dsm_result *res)
 {
+	acpi_handle handle = ACPI_HANDLE(rtwdev->dev);
 	union acpi_object *obj;
 	int ret;
 
-	obj = acpi_evaluate_dsm(ACPI_HANDLE(rtwdev->dev), &rtw89_guid,
-				0, func, NULL);
+	if (!handle || func >= 64 ||
+	    !acpi_check_dsm(handle, &rtw89_guid, 0, BIT_ULL(func))) {
+		rtw89_debug(rtwdev, RTW89_DBG_ACPI,
+			    "ACPI _DSM function %d unavailable\n", func);
+		return -ENOENT;
+	}
+
+	obj = acpi_evaluate_dsm(handle, &rtw89_guid, 0, func, NULL);
 	if (!obj) {
 		rtw89_debug(rtwdev, RTW89_DBG_ACPI,
 			    "acpi dsm fail to evaluate func: %d\n", func);
